<!-- MUSCLE GLYPH - CHEST. The upper body with the two pectorals drawn on it.

     ONE PART, drawn alone, in the equipment set's lane: stroke only, 1.8 wide, round
     caps and joins, nothing filled (owner, 2026-10-11: *"clean muscle group icons of
     body parts, arm leg etc etc ... remake them to actually match with the icons you
     drew for the equipments"*).

     Why the chest keeps the head while the back and the core do not: the two pectorals
     are the only thing in this glyph, and a pair of plates floating on their own is
     not a chest - it is a pair of goggles. The bust says WHERE, the pec arcs say WHAT.
     The back has a spine and a pair of shoulder blades to do that job, the core has its
     own divisions, so neither needs the context.

     It is also kept TALL (down to the waist) on purpose: the shoulder glyph beside it
     is the top of the same body, and at the 22dp the filter row draws, the two are
     told apart by silhouette - the bust is tall and narrow, the shoulder yoke is wide
     and flat. Every glyph is then centred in its own box by the same measurement the
     kit icons are: [MuscleGlyphFamilyTest] rasterises each one and requires its ink to
     clear all four edges, which is what caught this drawing sitting too high. -->
